qudtqk:Pressure qudt:latexDefinition "\\(p = \\frac{dF}{dA}\\), where \\(dF\\) is the force component perpendicular to the surface element of area \\(dA\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Illuminance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(E_v = \\frac{d\\Phi}{dA}\\), where \\(d\\Phi\\) is the luminous flux incident on an element of the surface with area \\(dA\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:VolumeFlowRate qudt:latexDefinition "\\(q_V = \\frac{dV}{dt}\\), where \\(V\\) is volume and \\(t\\) is time."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AngularFrequency qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\omega = 2\\pi f\\), where \\(f\\) is frequency."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:CAL_TH qudt:latexDefinition """\\(1 \\; cal_{th} = 4.184 J\\)

\\(\\approx 0.003964 BTU\\)

\\(\\approx 1.163 \\times 10^{-6} kWh\\)

\\(\\approx 2.611 \\times 10^{19} eV\\)"""^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:J qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\text{J}\\ \\equiv\\ \\text{joule}\\ \\equiv\\ \\text{CV}\\ \\equiv\\ \\text{coulomb.volt}\\ \\equiv\\ \\frac{\\text{eV}}{1.602\\ 10^{-19}}\\ \\equiv\\ \\frac{\\text{electron.volt}}{1.602\\ 10^{-19}}\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:PlanckEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(E_\\rho = \\sqrt{\\frac{ \\hbar c^5}{G}} \\approx 1.936 \\times 10^9 J \\approx 1.22 \\times 10^{28} eV \\approx 0.5433 MWh\\), where  \\(c\\) is the speed of light in a vacuum, \\(\\hbar\\) is the reduced Planck's constant, and \\(G\\) is the gravitational constant."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:ERG qudt:latexDefinition "\\(g\\cdot cm^{2}/s^{2}\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Frequency qudt:latexDefinition """\\(f = 1/T\\), where \\(T\\) is a period.

Alternatively,

\\(\\nu = 1/T\\)"""^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ActivityConcentration qudt:latexDefinition "\\(c_A = \\frac{A}{V}\\), where \\(A\\) is the activity of a sample and \\(V\\) is its volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Force qudt:latexDefinition "\\(F = \\frac{dp}{dt}\\), where \\(F\\) is the resultant force acting on a body, \\(p\\) is momentum of a body, and \\(t\\) is time."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MeanLifetime qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\tau = \\frac{1}{\\lambda}\\), where \\(\\lambda\\) is the decay constant."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpecificEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(e = E/m\\), where \\(E\\) is energy and \\(m\\) is mass."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Density qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\rho = m/V\\), where \\(\\rho\\) is the density, \\(m\\) is the mass, and \\(V\\) is the volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Stress qudt:latexDefinition "\\({\\rm{Stress}} = \\frac{F}{A}\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LinearMomentum qudt:latexDefinition "p = m\\upsilon"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RadiantIntensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(I = \\frac{d\\Phi}{d\\Omega}\\), where \\(d\\Phi\\) is the radiant flux leaving the source in an elementary cone containing the given direction with the solid angle \\(d\\Omega\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MomentOfInertia qudt:latexDefinition "\\(I_Q = \\int r^2_Q dm\\), where \\(r_Q\\) is the radial distance from a \\(Q-axis\\) and \\(m\\) is mass."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AngularMomentum qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L = I\\omega\\), where \\(I\\) is the moment of inertia, and \\(\\omega\\) is the angular velocity."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassPerArea qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\rho_A = \\frac {m} {A}\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Power qudt:latexDefinition "\\(P = F \\cdot v\\), where \\(F\\) is force and \\(v\\) is velocity."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:DynamicViscosity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\tau_{xz} = \\eta\\frac{dv_x}{dz}\\), where \\(\\tau_{xz}\\) is shear stress in a fluid moving with a velocity gradient \\(\\frac{dv_x}{dz}\\) perpendicular to the plane of shear. "^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Torque qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\tau = M \\cdot e_Q\\), where \\(M\\) is the momentof force and \\(e_Q\\) is a unit vector directed along a \\(Q-axis\\) with respect to which the torque is considered."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Resistance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(R = \\frac{u}{i}\\), where \\(u\\) is instantaneous voltage and \\(i\\) is instantaneous electric current."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:IsothermalCompressibility qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\varkappa_T = \\frac{1}{V}\\left (\\frac{\\partial V}{\\partial p} \\right )_T\\), where \\(V\\) is volume, \\(p\\) is \\(pressure\\), and \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Compressibility qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\chi = -(\\frac{1}{V})\\frac{dV}{d\\rho}\\), where \\(V\\) is volume and \\(p\\) is pressure."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:EarthMass qudt:latexDefinition """One Earth mass can be converted to related units:

81.3 Lunar mass (ML)
0.00315 Jupiter mass (MJ) (Jupiter has 317.83 Earth masses)[1]
0.0105 Saturn mass (Saturn has 95.16 Earth masses)[3]
0.0583 Neptune mass (Neptune has 17.147 Earth masses)[4]
0.000 003 003 Solar mass (\\(M_{\\odot}\\)) (The Sun has 332946 Earth masses)"""^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:PlanckMass qudt:latexDefinition "\\(m_P = \\sqrt{\\frac{ \\hbar c^3}{G}} \\approx 1.2209 \\times 10^{19} GeV/c^2 = 2.17651(13) \\times 10^{-8}\\), where \\(c\\) is the speed of light in a vacuum, \\(\\hbar\\) is the reduced Planck's constant, and \\(G\\) is the gravitational constant. The two digits enclosed by parentheses are the estimated standard error associated with the reported numerical value."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ThermalDiffusivity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(a = \\frac{\\lambda}{\\rho   c_\\rho}\\), where \\(\\lambda\\) is thermal conductivity, \\(\\rho\\) is mass density and \\(c_\\rho\\) is specific heat capacity at constant pressure."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ThermalInsulance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(M = 1/K\\), where \\(K\\) is \"Coefficient of Heat Transfer\""^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:CoefficientOfHeatTransfer qudt:latexDefinition """\"Coefficient of Heat Transfer\", in thermodynamics and in mechanical and chemical engineering, is used in calculating the heat transfer, typically by convection or phase transition between a fluid and a solid. The heat transfer coefficient is the proportionality coefficient between the heat flux, that is heat flow per unit area, \\(q/A\\), and the thermodynamic driving force for the flow of heat (that is, the temperature difference, \\( \\bigtriangleup T \\)).  Areic heat flow rate divided by thermodynamic temperature difference. In building technology, the \\(\\textit{Coefficient of Heat Transfer}\\), is often called \\(\\textit{thermal transmittance}\\), with the symbol \\(U\\). \\(\\textit{Coefficient of Heat Transfer}\\), has SI units in watts per squared meter kelvin: \\(W/(m^2 \\cdot K)\\) .

\\(K = \\frac{\\varphi}{T}\\), where \\(\\varphi\\) is areic heat flow rate and \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature difference."""^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Inductance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L =\\frac{\\Psi}{I}\\), where \\(I\\) is an electric current in a thin conducting loop, and \\(\\Psi\\) is the linked flux caused by that electric current."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricPotentialDifference qudt:latexDefinition "\\(V_{ab} = \\int_{r_a(C)}^{r_b} (E +\\frac{\\partial A}{\\partial t}) \\), where \\(E\\) is electric field strength, \\(A\\) is magentic vector potential,  \\(t\\) is time, and \\(r\\) is position vector along a curve C from a point \\(a\\) to \\(b\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricPotential qudt:latexDefinition "\\(-\\textbf{grad} \\; V = E + \\frac{\\partial A}{\\partial t}\\), where \\(E\\) is electric field strength, \\(A\\) is magentic vector potential and \\(t\\) is time."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Voltage qudt:latexDefinition "\\(U_{ab} = V_a - V_b\\), where \\(V_a\\) and \\(V_b\\) are electric potentials at points \\(a\\) and \\(b\\), respectively."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:V qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\text{V}\\ \\equiv\\ \\text{volt}\\ \\equiv\\ \\frac{\\text{J}}{\\text{C}}\\ \\equiv\\ \\frac{\\text{joule}}{\\text{coulomb}}\\ \\equiv\\ \\frac{\\text{W.s}}{\\text{C}}\\ \\equiv\\ \\frac{\\text{watt.second}}{\\text{coulomb}}\\ \\equiv\\ \\frac{\\text{W}}{\\text{A}}\\ \\equiv\\ \\frac{\\text{watt}}{\\text{amp}}\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SeebeckCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(S_{ab} = \\frac{dE_{ab}}{dT}\\), where \\(E_{ab}\\) is the thermosource voltage between substances a and b, \\(T\\) is the thermodynamic temperature of the hot junction."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Radiance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L = \\frac{dI}{dA}\\frac{1}{cos\\alpha}\\), where \\(dI\\) is the radiant intensity emitted from an element of the surface area \\(dA\\), and angle \\(\\alpha\\) is the angle between the normal to the surface and the given direction."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:IonicStrength qudt:latexDefinition "\\(I = \\frac{1}{2} \\sum z_i^2 b_i\\), where the summation is carried out over all ions with charge number \\(z_i\\) and molality \\(m_i\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Action qudt:latexDefinition "\\(S = \\int Ldt\\), where \\(L\\) is the Lagrange function and \\(t\\) is time."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ActivePower qudt:latexDefinition "\\(P = \\frac{1}{T}\\int_{0}^{T} pdt\\), where \\(T\\) is the period and \\(p\\) is instantaneous power."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:W qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\text{W}\\ \\equiv\\ \\text{watt}\\ \\equiv\\ \\frac{\\text{J}}{\\text{s}}\\ \\equiv\\ \\frac{\\text{joule}}{\\text{second}}\\ \\equiv\\ \\frac{\\text{N.m}}{\\text{s}}\\ \\equiv\\ \\frac{\\text{newton.metre}}{\\text{second}}\\ \\equiv\\ \\text{V.A}\\ \\equiv\\ \\text{volt.amp}\\ \\equiv\\ \\Omega\\text{.A}^{2}\\ \\equiv\\ \\text{ohm.amp}^{2}\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpectralCrossSection qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\sigma = \\int \\sigma_E dE\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MagneticVectorPotential qudt:latexDefinition "\\(B = \\textbf{rot} A\\), where \\(B\\) is magnetic flux density."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LagrangeFunction qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L(q_i, \\dot{q_i}) = T(q_i, \\dot{q_i}) - V(q_i)\\), where \\(T\\) is kinetic energy, \\(V\\) is potential energy, \\(q_i\\) is a generalized coordinate, and \\(\\dot{q_i}\\) is a generalized velocity."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:BARYE qudt:latexDefinition "\\(g/(cm\\cdot s{2}\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:ATM_T qudt:latexDefinition "\\(1 at = 98.0665 kPa \\approx 0.96784 standard atmospheres\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassAttenuationCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mu_m = \\frac{\\mu}{\\rho}\\), where \\(\\mu\\) is the linear attenuation coefficient and \\(\\rho\\) is the mass density of the medium."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ComplexPower qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\underline{S} = \\underline{U}\\underline{I^*}\\), where \\(\\underline{U}\\) is voltage phasor and \\(\\underline{I^*}\\) is the complex conjugate of the current phasor."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:PlanckLength qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\ell_P = \\sqrt{\\frac{ \\hbar G}{c^3}} \\approx 1.616199(97)) \\times 10^{-35} m\\), where \\(c\\) is the speed of light in a vacuum, \\(\\hbar\\) is the reduced Planck's constant, and \\(G\\) is the gravitational constant. The two digits enclosed by parentheses are the estimated standard error associated with the reported numerical value."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassFlowRate qudt:latexDefinition "\\(q_m = \\frac{dm}{dt}\\), where \\(m\\) is mass and \\(t\\) is time."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ExtentOfReaction qudt:latexDefinition "\\(dn_B = \\nu_B d\\xi\\), where \\(n_B\\) is the amount of substance \\(B\\) and \\(\\nu_B\\) is the stoichiometric number of substance \\(B\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:BulkModulus qudt:latexDefinition "\\(K = \\frac{p}{\\vartheta}\\), where \\(p\\) is pressure and \\(\\vartheta\\) is volume strain."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MolarVolume qudt:latexDefinition "\\(V_m = \\frac{V}{n}\\), where \\(V\\) is volume and \\(n\\) is amount of substance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MagneticFieldStrength_H qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mathbf{H} = \\frac{\\mathbf{B} }{\\mu_0} - M\\), where \\(\\mathbf{B} \\) is magnetic flux density, \\(\\mu_0\\) is the magnetic constant and \\(M\\) is magnetization."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Impedance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\underline{Z} = \\underline{U} / \\underline{I}\\), where \\(\\underline{U}\\) is the voltage phasor and \\(\\underline{I}\\) is the electric current phasor."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricCurrentPhasor qudt:latexDefinition "When \\(i = \\hat{I} \\cos{(\\omega t + \\alpha)}\\), where \\(i\\) is the electric current, \\(\\omega\\) is angular frequence, \\(t\\) is time, and \\(\\alpha\\) is initial phase, then \\(\\underline{I} = Ie^{ja}\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:VoltagePhasor qudt:latexDefinition "When \\(u = \\hat{U} \\cos{(\\omega t + \\alpha)}\\), where \\(u\\) is the voltage, \\(\\omega\\) is angular frequency, \\(t\\) is time, and \\(\\alpha\\) is initial phase, then \\(\\underline{U} = Ue^{ja}\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:DoseEquivalent qudt:latexDefinition "At the point of interest in tissue, \\(H = DQ\\), where \\(D\\) is the absorbed dose and \\(Q\\) is the quality factor at that point."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:PermittivityOfVacuum qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\epsilon = \\frac{\\mathbf{D}}{\\mathbf{E}}\\), where \\(\\mathbf{D}\\) is electric flux density and \\(\\mathbf{E}\\) is electric field strength."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricFieldStrength qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mathbf{E} = \\mathbf{F}/q\\), where \\(\\mathbf{F}\\) is force and \\(q\\) is electric charge, of a test particle at rest."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Permittivity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\epsilon = \\frac{D}{E}\\), where \\(D\\) is electric flux density and \\(E\\) is electric field strength."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricFluxDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mathbf{D}  = \\epsilon_0 E + P\\), where \\(\\epsilon_0\\) is the electric constant, \\(\\mathbf{E} \\) is electric field strength, and \\(P\\) is electric polarization."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:IntinsicCarrierDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(np = n_i^2\\), where \\(n\\) is electron density and \\(p\\) is hole density."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:NumberDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(n = \\frac{N}{V}\\), where \\(N\\) is the number of particles and \\(V\\) is volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MagneticFluxDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mathbf{F}  = qv \\times B\\), where \\(F\\) is force and \\(v\\) is velocity of any test particle with electric charge \\(q\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:FaradayConstant qudt:latexDefinition "\\(F = N_A e\\), where \\(N_A\\) is the Avogadro constant and \\(e\\) is the elementary charge."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SectionModulus qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Z = \\frac{I_a}{(r_Q)_{max}}\\), where \\(I_a\\) is the second axial moment of area and \\((r_Q)_{max}\\) is the maximum radial distance of any point in the surface considered from the \\(Q-axis\\) with respect to which \\(I_a\\) is defined."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Lethargy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(u = \\ln(\\frac{E_0}{E})\\), where \\(E_0\\) is a reference energy."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\rho = \\frac{dm}{dV}\\), where \\(m\\) is mass and \\(V\\) is volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ThermalDiffusionRatioCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(D_T  = kT \\cdot D\\), where \\(k_T\\) is the thermal diffusion ratio, and \\(D\\) is the diffusion coefficient."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricCharge qudt:latexDefinition "\\(dQ = Idt\\), where \\(I\\) is electric current."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:C_Stat qudt:latexDefinition "\\(1 C \\leftrightarrow 2997924580 statC \\approx 3.00 \\times 10^9 statC,\\ 1 \\hspace{0.3pc} statC \\leftrightarrow \\hspace{0.3pc} \\approx 3.34 \\times 10^{-10} C\\) for electric charge."^^qudt:LatexString,
    "\\(1 C \\leftrightarrow 4 \\pi \\times 2997924580 statC \\approx 3.77 \\times 10^{10} statC,\\ 1 \\hspace{0.3pc} statC \\leftrightarrow \\hspace{0.2pc} \\approx 2.6 \\times 10^{-11} C\\) for electric flux \\(\\Phi_D\\)"^^qudt:LatexString,
    "\\(1 C/m \\leftrightarrow 4 \\pi \\times 2997924580 \\times 10^{-4} statC/cm \\approx 3.77 \\times 10^6 statC/cm,\\ 1 \\hspace{0.3pc} statC/cm \\leftrightarrow \\hspace{0.3pc} \\approx 2.65 \\times 10^{-7} C/m\\) for electric displacement field \\(D\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:DisplacementVectorOfIon qudt:latexDefinition "\\(u = R - R_0\\), where \\(R\\) is the particle position vector and \\(R_0\\) is the equilibrium position vector of a particle."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectromagneticEnergyDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(w = (1/2) ( \\mathbf{E} \\cdot \\mathbf{D} + \\mathbf{B} \\cdot \\mathbf{H})\\), where \\(\\mathbf{E}\\) is electric field strength, \\(\\mathbf{D}\\) is electric flux density, \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) is magnetic flux density, and \\(\\mathbf{H}\\) is magnetic field strength."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:VolumicElectromagneticEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(w = (1/2) ( \\mathbf{E} \\cdot \\mathbf{D} + \\mathbf{B} \\cdot \\mathbf{H})\\), where \\(\\mathbf{E}\\) is electric field strength, \\(\\mathbf{D}\\) is electric flux density, \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) is magnetic flux density, and \\(\\mathbf{H}\\) is magnetic field strength."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpecificEntropy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(s = S/m\\), where \\(S\\) is entropy and \\(m\\) is mass."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AbsorbedDoseRate qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\dot{D} = \\frac{dD}{dt}\\), where \\(dD\\) is the increment of absorbed dose during time interval with duration \\(dt\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Resistivity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\rho = \\frac{1}{\\sigma}\\), if it exists, where \\(\\sigma\\) is conductivity."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ThermalConductivity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\lambda = \\frac{\\varphi}{T}\\), where \\(\\varphi\\) is areic heat flow rate and \\(T\\) is temperature gradient."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Capacitance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(C = Q/U\\), where \\(Q\\) is electric charge and \\(V\\) is voltage."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RelativeHumidity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\varphi = p / p_{sat}\\), where \\(p\\) is partial pressure of vapour,  \\(p_{sat}\\) is thermodynamic temperature and \\(V\\) is its partial pressure at saturation (at the same temperature). Relative partial pressure is often referred to as \\(RH\\) and expressed in percent. \\(\\textit{Relative Humidity}\\) is also referred to as \\(\\textit{Relative Partial Pressure}\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MobilityRatio qudt:latexDefinition "\\(b = \\frac{\\mu_n}{\\mu_p}\\), where \\(\\mu_n\\) and \\(\\mu_p\\) are mobilities for electrons and holes, respectively."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectromagneticPermeability qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mu = \\frac{B}{H}\\),  where \\(B\\) is magnetic flux density,  and \\(H\\) is magnetic field strength."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:DYN qudt:latexDefinition "\\(g\\cdot cm/s^{2}\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:BohrMagneton qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mu_B = \\frac{e\\hbar}{2m_e}\\), where \\(e\\) is the elementary charge, \\(\\hbar\\) is the Planck constant, and \\(m_e\\) is the rest mass of electron."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MagneticDipoleMoment qudt:latexDefinition """\\(E_m = -m \\cdot B\\), where \\(E_m\\) is the interaction energy of the molecule with magnetic diploe moment \\(m\\) and a magnetic field with magnetic flux density \\(B\\)

or,

\\(J_m = \\mu_0 M\\) where \\(\\mu_0\\) is the magnetic constant and \\(M\\) is Magnetization."""^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:ComptonWavelength qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\lambda_C = \\frac{h}{mc_0}\\), where \\(h\\) is the Planck constant, \\(m\\) is the rest mass of a particle, and \\(c_0\\) is the speed of light in vacuum."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpeedOfSound qudt:latexDefinition "\\(c = \\sqrt{\\frac{K}{\\rho}}\\), where \\(K\\) is the coefficient of stiffness, the bulk modulus (or the modulus of bulk elasticity for gases), and \\(\\rho\\) is the density. Also, \\(c^2 = \\frac{\\partial p}{\\partial \\rho}\\), where \\(p\\) is the pressure and \\(\\rho\\) is the density."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricCurrentDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(J = \\rho v\\), where \\(\\rho\\) is electric current density and \\(v\\) is volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:EquilibriumConstantOnConcentrationBasis qudt:latexDefinition "\\(K_c = \\Pi_B(c_B)^{-\\nu_B}\\), for solutions"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:EquilibriumConstant qudt:latexDefinition "\\(K^\\Theta = \\Pi_B(\\lambda_B^\\Theta)^{-\\nu_B}\\), where \\(\\Pi_B\\) denotes the product for all substances \\(B\\), \\(\\lambda_B^\\Theta\\) is the standard absolute activity of substance \\(B\\), and \\(\\nu_B\\) is the stoichiometric number of the substance \\(B\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RadiantEnergyDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(w\\), \\(\\rho = \\frac{dQ}{dV}\\), where \\(dQ\\) is the radiant energy in an elementary three-dimensional domain, and \\(dV\\) is the volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:CartesianArea qudt:latexDefinition "\\(A = \\int\\int dxdy\\), where \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) are cartesian coordinates."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SoundVolumeVelocity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(q= vS\\), where \\(v\\) is sound particle velocity and \\(S\\) is the surface area through which an acoustic wave of frequence \\(f\\) propagates."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MutualInductance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L_{mn} = \\frac{\\Psi_m}{I_n}\\), where \\(I_n\\) is an electric current in a thin conducting loop \\(n\\) and \\(\\Psi_m\\) is the linked flux caused by that electric current in another loop \\(m\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:TotalAtomicStoppingPower qudt:latexDefinition "\\(S_a = \\frac{S}{n}\\), where \\(S\\) is the total linear stopping power and \\(n\\) is the number density of the atoms in the substance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Work qudt:latexDefinition "\\(A = \\int Pdt\\), where \\(P\\) is power and \\(t\\) is time."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:MagneticConstant qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mu_0 = \\frac{\\overrightarrow{B}}{\\overrightarrow{H}}\\), where \\(\\overrightarrow{B}\\) is the B-Filed magnetic vector, and \\(\\overrightarrow{H}\\) is the H-Filed magnetic vector. The value of \\(\\mu_0\\) is \\(\\approx 1.256637e-6\\,H/M\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:ElectromagneticPermeabilityOfVacuum qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mu_0 = \\frac{\\overrightarrow{B}}{\\overrightarrow{H}}\\), where \\(\\overrightarrow{B}\\) is the B-Filed magnetic vector, and \\(\\overrightarrow{H}\\) is the H-Field magnetic vector. The value of \\(\\mu_0\\) is \\(\\approx 1.256637e-6\\,henry\\,per\\,metre\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Activity qudt:latexDefinition """\\(A = Z + N\\), where \\(Z\\) is the atomic number and \\(N\\) is the neutron number.

Variation \\(dN\\) of spontaneous number of nuclei \\(N\\) in a particular energy state, in a sample of radionuclide, due to spontaneous nuclear transitions from this state during an infinitesimal time interval, divided by its duration \\(dt\\), thus \\(A = -\\frac{dN}{dt}\\)."""^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpecificActivity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(a = \\frac{A}{m}\\), where \\(A\\) is the activity of a sample and \\(m\\) is its mass."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LinearElectricCurrentDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(J_s = \\rho_A v\\), where \\(\\rho_A\\) is surface density of electric charge and \\(v\\) is velocity."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SurfaceTension qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\gamma = \\frac{dF}{dl}\\), where \\(F\\) is the force component perpendicular to a line element in a surface and \\(l\\) is the length of the line element."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:PhaseSpeedOfSound qudt:latexDefinition "\\(c = \\frac{\\omega}{k} = \\lambda f\\), where \\(\\omega\\) is the angular frequency, \\(k\\) is angular wavenumber, \\(\\lambda\\) is the wavelength, and \\(f\\) is the frequency."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:MilliDEG_C qudt:latexDefinition "millieDegree Celsius"^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:DEG_C qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\,^{\\circ}{\\rm C}\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpecificGibbsEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(g = G/m\\), where \\(G\\) is Gibbs energy and \\(m\\) is mass."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpecificHelmholtzEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(a = A/m\\), where \\(A\\) is Helmholtz energy and \\(m\\) is mass."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpecificInternalEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(u = U/m\\), where \\(U\\) is thermodynamic energy and \\(m\\) is mass."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpecificEnthalpy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(h = H/m\\), where \\(H\\) is enthalpy and \\(m\\) is mass."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:PressureCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\beta = \\left (\\frac{\\partial p}{\\partial T} \\right )_V\\), where \\(p\\) is \\(pressure\\),  \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature and \\(V\\) is volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Enthalpy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(H = U + pV\\), where \\(U\\) is internal energy, \\(p\\) is pressure and \\(V\\) is volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:PlanckFunction qudt:latexDefinition """The Planck function, \\(B_{\\tilde{\\nu}}(T)\\), is given by:
\\(B_{\\nu}(T) = \\frac{2h c^2\\tilde{\\nu}^3}{e^{hc / k \\tilde{\\nu} T}-1}\\)
where, \\(\\tilde{\\nu}\\) is wavelength, \\(h\\) is Planck's Constant, \\(k\\) is Boltzman's Constant, \\(c\\) is the speed of light in a vacuum, \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature."""^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassieuFunction qudt:latexDefinition "\\(J = -A/T\\), where \\(A\\) is Helmholtz energy and \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RelativeMassRatioOfVapour qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\psi = x / x_{sat}\\), where \\(x\\) is mass ratio of water vapour to dry gas,  \\(x_{sat}\\) is its mass raio of water vapour to dry gas at saturation (at the same temperature)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:DebyeTemperature qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Theta_D = \\frac{\\hbar\\omega_D}{k}\\), where \\(k\\) is the Boltzmann constant, \\(\\hbar\\) is the reduced Planck constant, and \\(\\omega_D\\) is the Debye angular frequency."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:CentiM-PER-SEC qudt:latexDefinition "\\(cm/s\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MolarHeatCapacity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(C_m = \\frac{C}{n}\\), where \\(C\\) is heat capacity and \\(n\\) is amount of substance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RadiantExposure qudt:latexDefinition "\\(H = \\int_{0}^{\\Delta t}{E}{dt}\\), where \\(E\\) is the irradiance acting during the time interval with duration \\(\\Delta t\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:C_Ab-PER-CentiM2 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(abcoulomb/cm^2\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Exposure qudt:latexDefinition "For X-or gamma radiation, \\(X = \\frac{dQ}{dm}\\), where \\(dQ\\) is the absolute value of the mean total electric charge of the ions of the same sign produced in dry air when all the electrons and positrons liberated or created by photons in an element of air are completely stopped in air, and \\(dm\\) is the mass of that element."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricChargeDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\rho = \\frac{dQ}{dV}\\), where \\(Q\\) is electric charge and \\(V\\) is Volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:DynamicFrictionCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mu = \\frac{F}{N}\\), where \\(F\\) is the tangential component of the contact force and \\(N\\) is the normal component of the contact force between two sliding bodies."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricPower qudt:latexDefinition "\\(p = ui\\), where \\(u\\) is instantaneous voltage and \\(i\\) is instantaneous electric current."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:PositionVector qudt:latexDefinition "\\(r = \\overrightarrow{OP}\\), where \\(O\\) and \\(P\\) are two points in space."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:SUSCEPTIBILITY_ELEC qudt:latexDefinition "\\chi_{\\text{e}} = \\frac{{\\mathbf P}}{\\varepsilon_0{\\mathbf E}}"^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:SUSCEPTIBILITY_MAG qudt:latexDefinition "\\chi_\\text{v} = \\frac{\\mathbf{M}}{\\mathbf{H}}"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Luminance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L_v = \\frac{dI_v}{dA}\\), where \\(dI_v\\) is the luminous intensity of an element of the surface with the area \\(dA\\) of the orthogonal projection of this element on a plane perpendicular to the given direction."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Radius qudt:latexDefinition "\\(r = \\frac{d}{2}\\), where \\(d\\) is the circle diameter."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ExposureRate qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\dot{X} = \\frac{dX}{dt}\\), where \\(X\\) is the increment of exposure during time interval with duration \\(t\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:VolumeFraction qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\varphi_B = \\frac{x_B V_{m,B}^*}{\\sum x_i V_{m,i}^*}\\), where \\(V_{m,i}^*\\) is the molar volume of the pure substances \\(i\\) at the same temperature and pressure, \\(x_i\\) denotes the amount-of-substance fraction of substance \\(i\\), and \\(\\sum\\) denotes summation over all substances \\(i\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SoundExposure qudt:latexDefinition "\\(E = \\int_{t1}^{t2}p^2dt\\), where \\(t1\\) and \\(t2\\) are the starting and ending times for the integral and \\(p\\) is the sound pressure."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:HeatCapacity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(C = dQ/dT\\), where \\(Q\\) is amount of heat and \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassConcentration qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\rho_B = \\frac{m_B}{V}\\), where \\(m_B\\) is the mass of substance \\(B\\) and \\(V\\) is the volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LinearStrain qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\xi = \\frac{\\Delta l}{l_0}\\), where \\(\\Delta l\\) is the increase in length and \\(l_0\\) is the length in a reference state to be specified."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AbsorbedDose qudt:latexDefinition "\\(D = \\frac{d\\bar{\\varepsilon}}{dm}\\), where \\(d\\bar{\\varepsilon}\\) is the mean energy imparted by ionizing radiation to an element of irradiated matter with the mass \\(dm\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Admittance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Y = \\frac{1}{Z}\\), where \\(Z\\) is impedance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Conductance qudt:latexDefinition """\\(G = Re\\underline{Y}\\), where \\(\\underline{Y}\\) is admittance.

Alternatively:

\\(G = \\frac{1}{R}\\), where \\(R\\) is resistance."""^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectronRadius qudt:latexDefinition "\\(r_e = \\frac{e^2}{4\\pi m_e c_0^2}\\), where \\(e\\) is the elementary charge, \\(\\varepsilon_0\\) is the electric constant, item \\(m_e\\) is the rest mass of electrons, and \\(c_0\\) is the speed of light in vacuum."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:TotalLinearStoppingPower qudt:latexDefinition "\\(S = -\\frac{dE}{dx}\\), where \\(-dE\\) is the energy decrement in the \\(x-direction\\) along an elementary path with the length \\(dx\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassDefect qudt:latexDefinition "\\(B = Zm(^{1}\\textrm{H}) + Nm_n - m_a\\), where \\(Z\\) is the proton number of the atom, \\(m(^{1}\\textrm{H})\\) is atomic mass of \\(^{1}\\textrm{H}\\), \\(N\\) is the neutron number, \\(m_n\\) is the rest mass of the neutron, and \\(m_a\\) is the rest mass of the atom."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:CombinedNonEvaporativeHeatTransferCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(h = h_r + h_c + h_k\\), where \\(h_r\\) is the linear radiative heat transfer coefficient, \\(h_c\\) is the convective heat transfer coefficient, and \\(h_k\\) is the conductive heat transfer coefficient."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RelativePressureCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\alpha_p = \\frac{1}{p}\\left (\\frac{\\partial p}{\\partial T} \\right )_V\\), where \\(p\\) is \\(pressure\\),  \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature and \\(V\\) is volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassFractionOfWater qudt:latexDefinition "\\(w_{H_2o} = \\frac{u}{1+u}\\), where \\(u\\) is mass ratio of water to dry water."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassFractionOfDryMatter qudt:latexDefinition "\\(w_d= 1 - w_{h2o}\\), where \\(w_{h2o}\\) is mass fraction of water."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Conductivity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mathbf{J} = \\sigma \\mathbf{E}\\), where \\(\\mathbf{J}\\) is electric current density, and \\(\\mathbf{E}\\) is electric field strength."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:EquilibriumConstantOnPressureBasis qudt:latexDefinition "\\(K_p = \\Pi_B(p_B)^{-\\nu_B}\\), for gases"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:GyromagneticRatio qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mu = \\gamma J\\), where \\(\\mu\\) is the magnetic dipole moment, and \\(J\\) is the total angular momentum."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:PowerFactor qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\lambda = \\left | P \\right | / \\left | S \\right |\\), where \\(P\\) is active power and \\(S\\) is apparent power."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LinearEnergyTransfer qudt:latexDefinition "For ionizing charged particles, \\(L_\\Delta = \\frac{dE_\\Delta}{dl}\\), where \\(dE_\\Delta\\) is the mean energy lost in elctronic collisions locally to matter along a small path through the matter, minus the sum of the kinetic energies of all the electrons released with kinetic energies in excess of \\(\\Delta\\), and \\(dl\\) is the length of that path."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LarmorAngularFrequency qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\omega_L = \\frac{e}{2m_e}B\\), where \\(e\\) is the elementary charge, \\(m_e\\) is the rest mass of electron, and \\(B\\) is the magnetic flux density."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:GibbsEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(G = H - T \\cdot S\\), where \\(H\\) is enthalpy, \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature and \\(S\\) is entropy."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:HelmholtzEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(H = U - T \\cdot S\\), where \\(U\\) is internal energy, \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature and \\(S\\) is entropy."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:InternalEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "For a closed thermodynamic system, \\(\\Delta U = Q + W\\), where \\(Q\\) is amount of heat transferred to the system and \\(W\\) is work done on the system provided that no chemical reactions occur."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectromagneticWavePhaseSpeed qudt:latexDefinition "\\(c  = w/k\\) where \\(w\\) is angular velocity and \\(k\\) is angular wavenumber."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Reluctance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(R_m = \\frac{U_m}{\\Phi}\\), where \\(U_m\\) is magnetic tension, and \\(\\Phi\\) is magnetic flux."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MagneticFlux qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Phi = \\int_S B \\cdot e_n d A\\), over a surface \\(S\\), where \\(B\\) is magnetic flux density and \\(e_n dA\\) is the vector surface element."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MagneticTension qudt:latexDefinition "\\(U_m = \\int_{r_a(C)}^{r_b} \\mathbf{H} \\cdot dr\\), where \\(\\mathbf{H}\\) is magnetic field strength and \\(r\\) is the position vector along a given curve \\(C\\) from point \\(a\\) to point \\(b\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassRatioOfWaterToDryMatter qudt:latexDefinition "\\(u = m/m_d\\), where \\(m\\) is mass of water vapour and \\(m_d\\) is mass of dry matter. Mass ratio of water to dry matter at saturation is denoted \\(u_{sat}\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LandeGFactor qudt:latexDefinition "\\(g = \\frac{\\mu}{J\\mu_B}\\), where \\(\\mu\\) is the magnitude of magnetic dipole moment, \\(J\\) is the total angular momentum quantum number, and \\(\\mu_B\\) is the Bohr magneton."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ThermalConductance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(G = 1/R\\), where \\(R\\) is \"Thermal Resistance\""^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:StructureFactor qudt:latexDefinition "\\(F(h, k, l) = \\sum_{n=1}^N f_n\\exp{[2\\pi i(hx_n + ky_n +lz_n)]}\\), where \\(f_n\\) is the atomic scattering factor for atom \\(n\\), and \\(x_n\\), \\(y_n\\), and \\(z_n\\) are fractional coordinates in the unit cell; for \\(h\\), \\(k\\), and \\(l\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RadiantFluenceRate qudt:latexDefinition "\\(E_0 = \\int{L}{d\\Omega}\\), where \\(d\\Omega\\) is the solid angle of each elementary beam passing through the given point and \\(L\\) its radiance at that point in the direction of the beam."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:InstantaneousPower qudt:latexDefinition "\\(p = ui\\), where \\(u\\) is instantaneous voltage and \\(i\\) is instantaneous electric current."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:PlanckImpedance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Z_P = \\frac{V_P}{I_P}= \\frac{1}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0c}=\\frac{\\mu_oc}{4\\pi}=\\frac{Z_0}{4\\pi}=29.9792458\\Omega\\)\\where \\(V_P\\) is the Planck voltage, \\(I_P\\) is the Planck current, \\(c\\) is the speed of light in a vacuum, \\(\\epsilon_0\\) is the permittivity of free space, \\(\\mu_0\\) is the permeability of free space, and \\(Z_0\\) is the impedance of free space."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ReactivePower qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Q = lm \\underline{S}\\), where \\(\\underline{S}\\) is complex power. Alternatively expressed as: \\(Q = S \\cdot \\sin  \\psi\\), where \\(\\psi\\) is the displacement angle."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ActivityCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(f_B = \\frac{\\lambda_B}{(\\lambda_B^*x_B)}\\), where \\(\\lambda_B\\) the absolute activity of substance \\(B\\), \\(\\lambda_B^*\\) is the absolute activity of the pure substance \\(B\\) at the same temperature and pressure, and \\(x_B\\) is the amount-of-substance fraction of substance \\(B\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MolarConductivity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Gamma_m = \\frac{x}{c_B}\\), where \\(x\\) is the electrolytic conductivity and \\(c_B\\) is the amount-of-substance concentration."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:ERG-PER-SEC qudt:latexDefinition "\\(g\\cdot cm^{2}/s^{3}\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:PlanckPower qudt:latexDefinition "\\(P_p = {\\frac{ c^5}{G}}\\), where \\(c\\) is the speed of light in a vacuum, and \\(G\\) is the gravitational constant."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:TotalCurrentDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(J_{tot}= J + J_D\\), where \\(J\\) is electric current density and \\(J_D\\) is displacement current density."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:DisplacementCurrentDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(J_D = \\frac{\\partial D}{\\partial t}\\), where \\(D\\) is electric flux density and \\(t\\) is time."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RichardsonConstant qudt:latexDefinition "The thermionic emission current, \\(J\\), for a metal is \\(J = AT^2\\exp{(-\\frac{\\Phi}{kT})}\\), where \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature, \\(k\\) is the Boltzmann constant, and \\(\\Phi\\) is a work function."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Diameter qudt:latexDefinition "\\(d = 2r\\), where \\(r\\) is the radius of the circle."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RelativeMassDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(d = \\frac{\\rho}{\\rho_0}\\), where \\(\\rho\\) is mass density of a substance and \\(\\rho_0\\) is the mass density of a reference substance under conditions that should be specified for both substances."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:KinematicViscosity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\nu = \\frac{\\eta}{\\rho}\\), where \\(\\eta\\) is dynamic viscosity and \\(\\rho\\) is mass density."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MolarAbsorptionCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(x = aV_m\\), where \\(a\\) is the linear absorption coefficient and \\(V_m\\) is the molar volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MolarAttenuationCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mu_c = -\\frac{\\mu}{c}\\), where \\(\\mu\\) is the linear attenuation coefficient and \\(c\\) is the amount-of-substance concentration."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SoundParticleVelocity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(v = \\frac{\\partial\\delta }{\\partial t}\\), where \\(\\delta\\) is sound particle displacement and \\(t\\) is time."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:DecayConstant qudt:latexDefinition "Relative variation \\(\\frac{dN}{N}\\) of the number \\(N\\) of atoms or nuclei in a system, due to spontaneous emission from these atoms or nuclei during an infinitesimal time interval, divided by its duration \\(dt\\), thus \\(\\lambda = -\\frac{1}{N}\\frac{dN}{dt}\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ChemicalAffinity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(A = -\\sum \\nu_b\\mu_B\\), where \\(\\nu_b\\) is the stoichiometric number of substance \\(B\\) and \\(\\mu_B\\) is the chemical potential of substance \\(B\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:JosephsonConstant qudt:latexDefinition "\\(K_J = \\frac{1}{\\Phi_0}\\), where \\(\\Phi_0\\) is the magnetic flux quantum."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:FermiTemperature qudt:latexDefinition "\\(T_F = \\frac{E_F}{k}\\), where \\(E_F\\) is the Fermi energy and \\(k\\) is the Boltzmann constant."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:IsentropicCompressibility qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\varkappa_S = \\frac{1}{V}\\left (\\frac{\\partial V}{\\partial p} \\right )_S\\), where \\(V\\) is volume, \\(p\\) is \\(pressure\\), and \\(S\\) is entropy,"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AngularWavenumber qudt:latexDefinition """\\(k = \\frac{2\\pi}{\\lambda}= \\frac{2\\pi\\upsilon}{\\upsilon_p}=\\frac{\\omega}{\\upsilon_p}\\), where \\(\\upsilon\\) is the frequency of the wave, \\(\\lambda\\) is the wavelength, \\(\\omega = 2\\pi \\upsilon\\) is the angular frequency of the wave, and \\(\\upsilon_p\\) is the phase velocity of the wave.

Alternatively:

\\(k = \\frac{p}{\\hbar}\\), where \\(p\\) is the linear momentum of quasi free electrons in an electron gas and \\(\\hbar\\) is the reduced Planck constant (\\(h\\) divided by \\(2\\pi\\)); for phonons, its magnitude is \\(k = \\frac{2\\pi}{\\lambda}\\), where \\(\\lambda\\) is the wavelength of the lattice vibrations."""^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SphericalIlluminance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(E_v,0 = \\int_{4\\pi sr}{L_v}{d\\Omega}\\), where \\(d\\Omega\\) is the solid angle of each elementary beam passing through the given point and \\(L_v\\) is its luminance at that point in the direction of the beam."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SurfaceDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\rho_A = \\frac{dm}{dA}\\), where \\(m\\) is mass and \\(A\\) is area."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AtomScatteringFactor qudt:latexDefinition "\\(f = \\frac{E_a}{E_e}\\), where \\(E_a\\) is the radiation amplitude scattered by the atom and \\(E_e\\) is the radiation ampliture scattered by a single electron."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:DiffusionCoefficientForFluenceRate qudt:latexDefinition "\\(D_\\varphi = -\\frac{J_x}{\\frac{\\partial d\\varphi}{\\partial dx}}\\), where \\(J_x\\) is the \\(x-component\\) of the particle current and \\(\\varphi\\) is the particle fluence rate."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricChargeLinearDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\rho_l = \\frac{dQ}{dl}\\), where \\(Q\\) is electric charge and \\(l\\) is length."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:MolarGasConstant qudt:latexDefinition "\\(pV_m = RT\\), where \\(p\\) is pressure, \\(V_m\\) is molar volume, and \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LinearIonization qudt:latexDefinition "\\(N_{il} = \\frac{1}{e}\\frac{dQ}{dl}\\), where \\(e\\) is the elementary charge and \\(dQ\\) is the average total charge of all positive ions produced over an infinitesimal element of the path with length \\(dl\\) by an ionizing charged particle."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LinearAttenuationCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition """\\(\\mu = -\\frac{1}{J}\\frac{dJ}{dx}\\), where \\(J\\) is the magnitude of the current rate of a beam of particles parallel to the \\(x-direction\\).

Or:

\\(\\mu(\\lambda) = \\frac{1}{\\Phi_\\lambda(\\lambda)}\\frac{d\\Phi_\\lambda(\\lambda)}{dl}\\), where \\(\\frac{d\\Phi}{\\Phi}\\) is the relative decrease in the spectral radiant flux \\(\\Phi\\) of a collimated beam of electromagnetic radiation corresponding to the wavelength \\(\\lambda\\) during traversal of an infinitesimal layer of a medium and \\(dl\\) is the length traversed."""^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AttenuationCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(F(x) = Ae^{-\\alpha x} \\cos{[\\beta (x - x_0)]}\\), then \\(\\alpha\\) is the attenuation coefficient and \\(\\beta\\) is the phase coefficient."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LinearAbsorptionCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\alpha(\\lambda) = \\frac{1}{\\Phi_\\lambda(\\lambda)}\\frac{d\\Phi_\\lambda(\\lambda)}{dl}\\), where \\(\\frac{d\\Phi}{\\Phi}\\) is the relative decrease, caused by absorption, in the spectral radiant flux \\(\\Phi\\) of a collimated beam of electromagnetic radiation corresponding to the wavelength \\(\\lambda\\) during traversal of an infinitesimal layer of a medium and \\(dl\\) is the length traversed."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:PropagationCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\gamma = \\alpha + j\\beta\\), where \\(\\alpha\\) is the attenuation coefficient and \\(\\beta\\) is the phase coefficient."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:CurvatureFromRadius qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\kappa = \\frac{1}{\\rho}\\), where \\(\\rho\\) is the radius of the curvature."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:PhaseCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "If \\(F(x) = Ae^{-\\alpha x} \\cos{[\\beta (x - x_0)]}\\), then \\(\\alpha\\) is the attenuation coefficient and \\(\\beta\\) is the phase coefficient."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:NapierianAbsorbance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(A_e(\\lambda) = -ln(\\tau(\\lambda))\\), where \\(\\tau\\) is the transmittance at a given wavelength \\(\\lambda\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LorenzCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L = \\frac{\\lambda}{\\sigma T}\\), where \\(\\lambda\\) is thermal conductivity, \\(\\sigma\\) is electric conductivity, and \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricDipoleMoment qudt:latexDefinition """\\(E_p = -p \\cdot E\\), where \\(E_p\\) is the interaction energy of the molecule with electric dipole moment \\(p\\) and an electric field with electric field strength \\(E\\).

\\(p = q(r_+ - r_i)\\), where \\(r_+\\) and \\(r_-\\) are the position vectors to carriers of electric charge \\(a\\) and \\(-q\\), respectively."""^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MagnetomotiveForce qudt:latexDefinition "\\(F_m = \\oint \\mathbf{H} \\cdot dr\\), where \\(\\mathbf{H}\\) is magnetic field strength and \\(r\\) is position vector along a given curve \\(C\\) from point \\(a\\) to point \\(b\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricFlux qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Psi = \\int_S D \\cdot e_n dA\\), over a surface \\(S\\), where \\(D\\) is electric flux density and \\(e_n dA\\) is the vector surface element."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MagneticMoment qudt:latexDefinition "\\(m = I e_n A\\), where \\(I\\) is electric current in a small closed loop, \\(e_n\\) is a unit vector perpendicular to the loop, and \\(A\\) is the area of the loop. The magnetic moment of a substance within a domain is the vector sum of the magnetic moments of all entities included in the domain."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MagneticAreaMoment qudt:latexDefinition "\\(m = I e_n A\\), where \\(I\\) is electric current in a small closed loop, \\(e_n\\) is a unit vector perpendicular to the loop, and \\(A\\) is the area of the loop. The magnetic moment of a substance within a domain is the vector sum of the magnetic moments of all entities included in the domain."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ParticleFluence qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Phi = \\frac{dN}{dA}\\), where \\(dN\\) describes the number of particles incident on a small spherical domain at a given point in space, and \\(dA\\) describes the cross-sectional area of that domain."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LogarithmicFrequencyInterval qudt:latexDefinition "\\(G = \\log_{2}(f2/f1)\\), where \\(f1\\) and \\(f2 \\geq f1\\) are frequencies of two tones."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MeanEnergyImparted qudt:latexDefinition "To the matter in a given domain, \\(\\bar{\\varepsilon} = R_{in} - R_{out} + \\sum Q\\), where \\(R_{in}\\) is the radiant energy of all those charged and uncharged ionizing particles that enter the domain, \\(R_{out}\\) is the radiant energy of all those charged and uncharged ionizing particles that leave the domain, and \\(\\sum Q\\) is the sum of all changes of the rest energy of nuclei and elementary particles that occur in that domain."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RadialDistance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(d = \\sqrt{r_1^2 + r_2^2 -2r_1r_2\\cos{(\\theta_1 - \\theta_2)}}\\), where \\(P_1\\) and \\(P_2\\) are two points with polar coordinates \\((r_1, \\theta_1)\\) and \\((r_2, \\theta_2)\\), respectively, and \\(d\\) is the distance."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:GT qudt:latexDefinition "\\({ GT=V\\times (0.2+0.02\\times \\log _{10}(V))}\\) where V is measured in cubic meters."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassEnergyTransferCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\frac{\\mu_{tr}}{\\rho} = -\\frac{1}{\\rho}\\frac{1}{R}\\frac{dR_{tr}}{dl}\\), where \\(dR_{tr}\\) is the mean energy that is transferred to kinetic energy of charged particles by interactions of the incident radiation \\(R\\) in traversing a distance \\(dl\\) in the material of density \\(\\rho\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AbsoluteActivity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\lambda_B = e^{\\frac{\\mu_B}{RT}}\\), where \\(\\mu_B\\) is the chemical potential of substance \\(B\\), \\(R\\) is the molar gas constant, and \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:EnergyDensityOfStates qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\rho(E) = n_E(E) = \\frac{dN(E)}{dE}\\frac{1}{V}\\), where \\(N(E)\\) is the total number of states with energy less than \\(E\\), and \\(V\\) is the volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassAbsorptionCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(a_m = \\frac{a}{\\rho}\\), where \\(a\\) is the linear absorption coefficient and \\(\\rho\\) is the mass density of the medium."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:SpeedOfLight_Vacuum qudt:latexDefinition "\\(c_0 = 1 / \\sqrt{\\epsilon_0 \\mu_0}\\), where {\\epsilon_0} is the permittivity of vacuum, and \\(\\mu_0\\) is the magnetic constant."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RadianceFactor qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\beta = \\frac{L_n}{L_d}\\), where \\(L_n\\) is the radiance of a surface element in a given direction and \\(L_d\\) is the radiance of the perfect reflecting or transmitting diffuser identically irradiated and viewed. Reflectance factor is equivalent to radiance factor or luminance factor (when the cone angle is infinitely small, and is equivalent to reflectance when the cone angle is \\(2π sr\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:IonTransportNumber qudt:latexDefinition "\\(t_B = \\frac{i_B}{i}\\), where \\(i_B\\) is the electric current carried by the ion \\(B\\) and \\(i\\) is the total electric current."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RelativeMassDefect qudt:latexDefinition "\\(B_r = \\frac{B}{m_u}\\), where \\(B\\) is the mass defect and \\(m_u\\) is the unified atomic mass constant."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RelativeMassConcentrationOfVapour qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\varphi = v / v_{sat}\\), where \\(v\\) is mass concentration of water vapour,  \\(v_{sat}\\) is its mass concentration of water vapour at saturation (at the same temperature). For normal cases, the relative partial pressure may be assumed to be equal to relative mass concentration of vapour."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RelativePartialPressure qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\varphi = p / p_{sat}\\), where \\(p\\) is partial pressure of vapour,  \\(p_{sat}\\) is thermodynamic temperature and \\(V\\) is its partial pressure at saturation (at the same temperature). Relative partial pressure is often referred to as \\(RH\\) and expressed in percent. \\(\\textit{Relative Partial Pressure}\\) is also referred to as \\(\\textit{Relative Humidity}\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:StaticFrictionCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mu = \\frac{F_max}{N}\\), where \\(F_max\\) is the maximum tangential component of the contact force and \\(N\\) is the normal component of the contact force between two bodies at relative rest."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L-4I0M-2H0T4D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^-4 M^-2 T^4\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 4 .

qkdv:A0E0L1.5I0M0.5TE0TM-1D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^1.5 M^0.5 T^-1\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime -1 .

qudtqk:Permeance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Lambda = \\frac{1}{R_m}\\), where \\(R_m\\) is reluctance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ShearStrain qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\gamma = \\frac{\\Delta x}{d}\\), where \\(\\Delta x\\) is the parallel displacement between two surfaces of a layer of thickness \\(d\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpecificVolume qudt:latexDefinition "\\(sv = \\frac{1}{\\rho}\\), where \\(\\rho\\) is mass density."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L3I0M-1H0T0D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^3 M^-1\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 0 .

qudtqk:LuminousFlux qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Phi_v = K_m \\int_{0}^{\\infty}{\\Phi_\\lambda(\\lambda)}{V(\\lambda)d\\lambda}\\), where \\(K_m\\) is the maximum spectral luminous efficacy, \\(\\Phi_\\lambda(\\lambda)\\) is the spectral radiant flux, \\(V(\\lambda)\\) is the spectral luminous efficiency, and \\(\\lambda\\) is the wavelength."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MolarEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(U_m = \\frac{U}{n}\\), where \\(U\\) is internal energy and \\(n\\) is amount of substance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricDisplacement qudt:latexDefinition "\\(D = \\epsilon_0 E + P\\), where \\(\\epsilon_0\\) is the electric constant, \\(E\\) is electric field strength, and \\(P\\) is electric polarization."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LuminousEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Q_v = \\int_{0}^{\\Delta t}{\\Phi_v}{dt}\\), where \\(\\Phi_v\\) is the luminous flux occurring during the time interval with duration \\(\\Delta t\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LuminousEfficacy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(K = \\frac{\\Phi_v}{\\Phi}\\), where \\(\\Phi_v\\) is the luminous flux and \\(\\Phi\\) is the corresponding radiant flux."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Magnetization qudt:latexDefinition "\\(M = dm/dV\\), where \\(m\\) is magentic moment of a substance in a domain with Volume \\(V\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectrolyticConductivity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(x = \\frac{J}{E}\\), where \\(J\\) is the electrolytic current density and \\(E\\) is the electric field strength."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:PER-PlanckMass2 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(m_P = \\sqrt{\\frac{ \\hbar c^3}{G}} \\approx 1.2209 \\times 10^{19} GeV/c^2 = 2.17651(13) \\times 10^{-8}\\), where \\(c\\) is the speed of light in a vacuum, \\(\\hbar\\) is the reduced Planck's constant, and \\(G\\) is the gravitational constant. The two digits enclosed by parentheses are the estimated standard error associated with the reported numerical value."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ParticleNumberDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(n = \\frac{N}{V}\\), where \\(N\\) is the number of particles in the 3D domain with the volume \\(V\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MagneticSusceptability qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\kappa = \\frac{M}{H}\\),  where \\(M\\) is magnetization,  and \\(H\\) is magnetic field strength."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:IonDensity qudt:latexDefinition """\\(n^+ = \\frac{N^+}{V}\\), \\(n^- = \\frac{N^-}{V}\\)

where \\(N^+\\) and \\(N^-\\) are the number of positive and negative ions, respectively, in a 3D domain with volume \\(V\\)."""^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:NeutronDiffusionCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(D_n = -\\frac{J_x}{\\frac{\\partial dn}{\\partial dx}}\\), where \\(J_x\\) is the \\(x-component\\) of the particle current and \\(n\\) is the particle number density."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:KermaRate qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\dot{K} = \\frac{dK}{dt}\\), where \\(K\\) is the increment of kerma during time interval with duration \\(t\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SoundPower qudt:latexDefinition "\\(P_a = IA\\), where \\(I\\) is the sound intensity in \\(\\frac{W}{m^2}\\) and \\(A\\) is the area in \\(m^2\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ActiveEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(W = \\int_{t_1}^{t_2} p dt\\), where \\(p\\) is instantaneous power and the integral interval is the time interval from \\(t_1\\) to \\(t_2\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AmountOfSubstanceFractionOfB qudt:latexDefinition "\\(x_B = \\frac{n_B}{n}\\), where \\(n_B\\) is the amount of substance \\(B\\) and \\(n\\) is the total amount of substance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L-2I1M0H0T0D1 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(U L^-2 J\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 1;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 0 .

qudtqk:SurfaceActivityDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(a_s = \\frac{A}{S}\\), where \\(S\\) is the total area of the surface of a sample and \\(A\\) is its activity."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:TotalMassStoppingPower qudt:latexDefinition "\\(S_m = \\frac{S}{\\rho}\\), where \\(S\\) is the total linear stopping power and \\(\\rho\\) is the mass density of the sample."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RadiantEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Q_e\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:NormalStress qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\sigma = \\frac{dF_n}{dA}\\), where \\(dF_n\\) is the normal component of force and \\(dA\\) is the area of the surface element."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ScalarMagneticPotential qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mathbf{H} = -grad V_m\\), where \\(\\mathbf{H}\\) is magnetic field strength."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LevelWidth qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Gamma = \\frac{\\hbar}{\\tau}\\), where \\(\\hbar\\) is the reduced Planck constant and \\(\\tau\\) is the mean lifetime."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Reactance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(X = im \\underline{Z}\\), where \\(\\underline{Z}\\) is impedance and \\(im\\) denotes the imaginary part."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L0I0M0H1T1D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(T Θ\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 1 .

qudtqk:MassExcess qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Delta = m_a - Am_u\\), where \\(m_a\\) is the rest mass of the atom, \\(A\\) is its nucleon number, and \\(m_u\\) is the unified atomic mass constant."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Absorptance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\alpha = \\frac{\\Phi_a}{\\Phi_m}\\), where \\(\\Phi_a\\) is the absorbed radiant flux or the absorbed luminous flux, and \\(\\Phi_m\\) is the radiant flux or luminous flux of the incident radiation."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:DiffusionLength qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L = \\sqrt{L^2}\\), where \\(L^2\\) is the diffusion area."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:CanonicalPartitionFunction qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Z = \\sum_r e^{-\\frac{E_r}{kT}}\\), where the sum is over all quantum states consistent with given energy, volume, external fields, and content, \\(E_r\\) is the energy in the \\(rth\\) quantum state, \\(k\\) is the Boltzmann constant, and \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L2I0M0H0T0D1 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(U L^2\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 0 .

qudtqk:RecombinationCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(-\\frac{dn^+}{dt} = -\\frac{dn^-}{dt} = an^+n^-\\), where \\(n^+\\) and \\(n^-\\) are the ion number densities of positive and negative ions, respectively, recombined during an infinitesimal time interval with duration \\(dt\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:A_Ab qudt:latexDefinition "\\(1\\,abA = 10\\,A\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A-1E0L3I0M1H0T-2D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^3 M T^-2 N^-1\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime -2 .

qudtqk:ModulusOfAdmittance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Y = \\left | \\underline{Y} \\right |\\), where \\(\\underline{Y}\\) is admittance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MolarOpticalRotatoryPower qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\alpha_n = \\alpha \\frac{A}{n}\\), where \\(\\alpha\\) is the angle of optical rotation, and \\(n\\) is the amount of substance of the optically active component in the path of a linearly polarized light beam of cross sectional area \\(A\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E-1L3I0M1H0T-3D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^3 M T^-3 I^-1\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent -1;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime -3 .

qudtqk:GeneralizedForce qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\delta A = \\sum Q_i\\delta q_i\\), where \\(A\\) is work and \\(q_i\\) is a generalized coordinate."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MomentOfForce qudt:latexDefinition "\\(M = r \\cdot F\\), where \\(r\\) is the position vector and \\(F\\) is the force."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:GrandCanonicalPartitionFunction qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Xi = \\sum_{N_A, N_B, ...} Z(N_A, N_B, ...) \\cdot \\lambda_A^{N_A} \\cdot \\lambda_B^{N_B} \\cdot ...\\), where \\(Z(N_A, N_B, ...)\\) is the canonical partition function for the given number of particles \\(A, B, ...,\\), and \\(\\lambda_A, \\lambda_B, ...\\) are the absolute activities of particles \\(A, B, ...\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SoundPowerLevel qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L_W = 10 \\log_{10} \\frac{P}{P_0} dB\\), where \\(P\\) is sound power and the reference value is \\(P_0 =1pW\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SoundExposureLevel qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L_E = 10 \\log_{10} \\frac{E}{E_0} dB\\), where \\(E\\) is sound power and the reference value is \\(E_0 = 400 \\mu Pa^2 s\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SoundReductionIndex qudt:latexDefinition "\\(R = 10 \\log (\\frac{1}{\\tau}) dB\\), where \\(\\tau\\) is the transmission factor."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SoundPressureLevel qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L_P = 10 \\log_{10} \\frac{p^2}{p_0^2} dB\\), where \\(p\\) is sound pressure and the reference value in airborne acoustics is \\(p_0 = 20 \\mu Pa\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ParticleCurrent qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\int J \\cdot e_n dA = \\frac{dN}{dt}\\), where \\(e_ndA\\) is the vector surface element, \\(N\\) is the net number of particles passing over a surface, and \\(dt\\) describes the time interval."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LinearExpansionCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\alpha_l = \\frac{1}{l} \\; \\frac{dl}{dT}\\), where \\(l\\) is \\(length\\) and \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MagneticPolarization qudt:latexDefinition "\\(J_m = \\mu_0 M\\),  where \\(\\mu_0\\) is the magentic constant and \\(M\\) is magnetization."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E1L0I0M0H0T0D-1 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(U^-1 I\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 1;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 0 .

qudtqk:ApparentPower qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\left | \\underline{S} \\right | =  UI\\), where \\(U\\) is rms value of voltage and \\(I\\) is rms value of electric current."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:VisibleRadiantEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "Q"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ThermodynamicCriticalMagneticFluxDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(G_n - G_s = \\frac{1}{2}\\frac{B_c^2 \\cdot V}{\\mu_0}\\), where \\(G_n\\) and \\(G_s\\) are the Gibbs energies at zero magnetic flux density in a normal conductor and superconductor, respectively, \\(\\mu_0\\) is the magnetic constant, and \\(V\\) is volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E1L1I0M0H0T1D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L T I\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 1;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 1 .

qudtqk:SpectralAngularCrossSection qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\sigma = \\int \\int \\sigma_{\\Omega,E} d\\Omega dE\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AngularCrossSection qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\sigma = \\int \\sigma_\\Omega d\\Omega\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SecondAxialMomentOfArea qudt:latexDefinition "\\(I_a = \\int r^2_Q dA\\), where \\(r_Q\\) is the radial distance from a \\(Q-axis\\) and \\(A\\) is area."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L4I0M0H0T0D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^4\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 0 .

qudtqk:EnergyFluence qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Psi = \\frac{dR}{dA}\\), where \\(dR\\) describes the sum of radiant energies, exclusive of rest energy, of all particles incident on a small spherical domain, and \\(dA\\) describes the cross-sectional area of that domain."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RadiantFluence qudt:latexDefinition "\\(H_0 = \\int_{0}^{\\Delta t}{E_0}{dt}\\), where \\(E_0\\) is the spherical radiance acting during time interval with duration \\(\\Delta t\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Wavelength qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\lambda = \\frac{c}{\\nu}\\), where \\(\\lambda\\) is the wave length, \\(\\nu\\) is the frequency, and \\(c\\) is the speed of light in the medium."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ThermalDiffusionFactor qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\alpha_T = \\frac{k_T}{(x_A x_B)}\\), where \\(k_T\\) is the thermal diffusion ratio, and \\(x_A\\) and \\(x_B\\) are the local amount-of-substance fractions of the two substances \\(A\\) and \\(B\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ThermalDiffusionRatio qudt:latexDefinition "In a steady state of a binary mixture in which thermal diffusion occurs, \\(grad x_B  = -(\\frac{k_T}{T}) grad T\\), where \\(x_B\\) is the amount-of-substance fraction of the heavier substance \\(B\\), and \\(T\\) is the local thermodynamic temperature."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:TotalCurrent qudt:latexDefinition "\\(I_{tot}= I + I_D\\), where \\(I\\) is electric current and \\(I_D\\) is displacement current."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:DisplacementCurrent qudt:latexDefinition "\\(I_D= \\int_S J_D \\cdot e_n dA\\), over a surface \\(S\\), where \\(J_D\\) is displacement current density and \\(e_n dA\\) is the vector surface element."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:TotalIonization qudt:latexDefinition "\\(N = \\int N_i dl\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L2I0M0H1T0D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^2 Θ\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 0 .

qkdv:A0E1L0I0M-1H1T2D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(M^-1 T^2 I Θ\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 1;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 2 .

qudtqk:ElectricChargeSurfaceDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\rho_A = \\frac{dQ}{dA}\\), where \\(Q\\) is electric charge and \\(A\\) is Area."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassRatioOfWaterVapourToDryGas qudt:latexDefinition "\\(x = m/m_d\\), where \\(m\\) is mass of water vapour and \\(m_d\\) is mass of dry gas. Mass ratio of water vapour to dry gas  at saturation is denoted \\(x_{sat}\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L4I0M2H0T-4D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^4 M^2 T^-4\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime -4 .

constant:ElectronGyromagneticRatio qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mu = \\gamma_e J\\), where \\(\\mu\\) is the magnetic dipole moment, and \\(J\\) is the total angular momentum."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:CubicExpansionCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\alpha_V = \\frac{1}{V} \\; \\frac{dV}{dT}\\), where \\(V\\) is \\(volume\\) and \\(T\\) is thermodynamic temperature."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:GeneralizedVelocity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\dot{q_i} = \\frac{dq_i}{dt}\\), where \\(q_i\\) is the generalized coordinate and \\(t\\) is time."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:CartesianVolume qudt:latexDefinition "\\(V = \\int\\int\\int dxdydz\\), where \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\) are cartesian coordinates."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:TransmittanceDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(A_{10}(\\lambda) = -lg(\\tau(\\lambda))\\), where \\(\\tau\\) is the transmittance at a given wavelength \\(\\lambda\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Susceptance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(B = \\lim{\\underline{Y}}\\), where \\(\\underline{Y}\\) is admittance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpectralLuminousEfficiency qudt:latexDefinition "\\(V(\\lambda) = \\frac{\\Phi_\\lambda(\\lambda_m)}{\\Phi_\\lambda(\\lambda)}\\), where \\(\\Phi_\\lambda(\\lambda_m)\\) is the spectral radiant flux at wavelength \\(\\lambda_m\\) and \\(\\Phi_\\lambda(\\lambda)\\) is the spectral radiant flux at wavelength \\(\\lambda\\), such that both radiations produce equal luminous sensations under specified photometric conditions and \\(\\lambda_m\\) is chosen so that the maximum value of this ratio is equal to 1."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:BendingMomentOfForce qudt:latexDefinition "\\(M_b = M \\cdot e_Q\\), where \\(M\\) is the momentof force and \\(e_Q\\) is a unit vector directed along a \\(Q-axis\\) with respect to which the torque is considered."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricSusceptibility qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\chi = \\frac{P}{(\\epsilon_0 E)}\\), where \\(P\\) is electric polorization, \\(\\epsilon_0\\) is the electric constant, and \\(E\\) is electric field strength."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SoundParticleAcceleration qudt:latexDefinition "\\(a = \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial t}\\), where \\(v\\) is sound particle velocity and \\(t\\) is time."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:GeneralizedCoordinate qudt:latexDefinition "\\(q_i\\), where \\(q_i\\) is one of the coordinates that is used to describe the position of the system under consideration, and \\(N\\) is the lowest number of coordinates necessary to fully define the position of the system."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ReflectanceFactor qudt:latexDefinition "\\(R = \\frac{\\Phi_n}{\\Phi_d}\\), where \\(\\Phi_n\\) is the radiant flux or luminous flux reflected in the directions delimited by a given cone and \\(\\Phi_d\\) is the flux reflected in the same directions by an identically radiated diffuser of reflectance equal to 1."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:NonActivePower qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Q^{'} = \\sqrt{{\\left | \\underline{S} \\right |}^2 - P^2}\\), where \\(\\underline{S}\\) is apparent power and \\(P\\) is active power."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Efficiency qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\eta = \\frac{P_{out}}{P_{in}}\\), where \\(P_{out}\\) is the output power and \\(P_{in}\\) is the input power."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ShearStress qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\tau = \\frac{dF_t}{dA}\\), where \\(dF_t\\) is the tangential component of force and \\(dA\\) is the area of the surface element."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:CelsiusTemperature qudt:latexDefinition """\"Celsius Temperature\", the thermodynamic temperature \\(T_0\\), is exactly \\(0.01\\)kelvin below the thermodynamic temperature of the triple point of water.
\\(t = T - T_0\\), where \\(T\\) is Thermodynamic Temperature and \\(T_0 = 273.15 K\\)."""^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RadiantFlux qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Phi = \\frac{dQ}{dt}\\), where \\(dQ\\) is the radiant energy emitted, transferred, or received during a time interval of the duration \\(dt\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SecondPolarMomentOfArea qudt:latexDefinition "\\(I_p = \\int r^2_Q dA\\), where \\(r_Q\\) is the radial distance from a \\(Q-axis\\) and \\(A\\) is area."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ShearModulus qudt:latexDefinition "\\(G = \\frac{\\tau}{\\gamma}\\), where \\(\\tau\\) is the shear stress and \\(\\gamma\\) is the shear strain."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:PermittivityRatio qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\epsilon_r = \\epsilon / \\epsilon_0\\), where \\(\\epsilon\\) is permittivity and \\(\\epsilon_0\\) is the electric constant."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ThermodynamicEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "For a closed thermodynamic system, \\(\\Delta U = Q + W\\), where \\(Q\\) is amount of heat transferred to the system and \\(W\\) is work done on the system provided that no chemical reactions occur."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LeakageFactor qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\sigma = 1 - k^2\\), where \\(k\\) is the coupling factor."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Transmittance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\tau = \\frac{\\Phi_t}{\\Phi_m}\\), where \\(\\Phi_t\\) is the transmitted radiant flux or the transmitted luminous flux, and \\(\\Phi_m\\) is the radiant flux or luminous flux of the incident radiation."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:PoyntingVector qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mathbf{S} = \\mathbf{E}  \\times \\mathbf{H} \\), where \\(\\mathbf{E}\\) is electric field strength and \\mathbf{H}  is magnetic field strength."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:CouplingFactor qudt:latexDefinition "For inductive coupling between two inductive elements, \\(k = \\frac{\\left | L_{mn} \\right |}{\\sqrt{L_m L_n}}\\), where \\(L_m\\) and \\(L_n\\) are their self inductances, and \\(L_{mn}\\) is their mutual inductance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ModulusOfImpedance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Z = \\left | \\underline{Z} \\right |\\), where \\(\\underline{Z}\\) is impedance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MechanicalSurfaceImpedance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Z_m = Z_a A^2\\), where \\(A\\) is the area of the surface considered and \\(Z_a\\) is the acoustic impedance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:EinsteinTransitionProbability qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\frac{-dN_j}{dt} = A_jkN_j\\), where \\(-dN_j\\) is the number of molecules spontaneously leaving the state j for the state k during a time interval of duration \\(dt\\), \\(N_j\\) is the number of molecules in the state j, and \\(E_j > E_k\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RefractiveIndex qudt:latexDefinition "\\(n = \\frac{c_0}{c}\\), where \\(c_0\\) is the speed of light in vacuum, and \\(c\\) is the speed of light in the medium."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MechanicalEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(E = T + V\\), where \\(T\\) is kinetic energy and \\(V\\) is potential energy."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LossFactor qudt:latexDefinition "\\(d = \\frac{1}{Q}\\), where \\(Q\\) is quality factor."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Reflectance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\rho = \\frac{\\Phi_t}{\\Phi_m}\\), where \\(\\Phi_t\\) is the reflected radiant flux, the reflected luminous flux, or the reflected sound power and \\(\\Phi_m\\) is the incident radiant flux, incident luminous flux, or incident sound power, respectively."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:QualityFactor qudt:latexDefinition "If \\(\\underline{Z} = R + jX\\), then \\(Q = \\left | X \\right |/R\\), where \\(\\underline{Z}\\) is impedance, \\(R\\) is resistance, and \\(X\\) is reactance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RatioOfSpecificHeatCapacities qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\gamma = c_p / c_V\\), where \\(c\\) is the specific heat of a gas, \\(c_p\\) is specific heat capacity at constant pressure, \\(c_V\\) is specific heat capacity at constant volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SoundEnergyDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(E = \\frac{I}{c}\\), where \\(I\\) is the sound intensity in \\(\\frac{W}{m^2}\\) and \\(c\\) is the sound speed in \\(\\frac{m}{s}\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:HamiltonFunction qudt:latexDefinition "\\(H = \\sum p_i\\dot{q_i} - L\\), where \\(p_i\\) is a generalized momentum, \\(\\dot{q_i}\\) is a generalized velocity, and \\(L\\) is the Lagrange function."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassConcentrationOfWater qudt:latexDefinition "\\(w = m/V\\), where \\(m\\) is mass of water, irrespective of the form of aggregation, and \\(V\\) is volume. Mass concentration of water at saturation is denoted \\(w_{sat}\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:VolumeStrain qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\vartheta = \\frac{\\Delta V}{V_0}\\), where \\(\\Delta V\\) is the increase in volume and \\(V_0\\) is the volume in a reference state to be specified."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AcousticImpedance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Z_a= \\frac{p}{q} = \\frac{p}{vS}\\), where \\(p\\) is the sound pressure, \\(q\\) is the sound volume velocity, \\(v\\) is sound particle velocity, and \\(S\\) is the surface area through which an acoustic wave of frequence \\(f\\) propagates."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Displacement qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Delta r =  R_f - R_i\\), where \\(R_f\\) is the final position and \\(R_i\\) is the initial position."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:GeneralizedMomentum qudt:latexDefinition "\\(p_i = \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial \\dot{q_i}}\\), where \\(L\\) is the Langrange function and \\(\\dot{q_i}\\) is a generalized velocity."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassConcentrationOfWaterVapour qudt:latexDefinition "\\(w = m/V\\), where \\(m\\) is mass of water vapour and \\(V\\) is total gas volume. Mass concentration of water vapour at saturation is denoted \\(v_{sat}\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:PhaseDifference qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\varphi = \\varphi_u - \\varphi_i\\), where \\(\\varphi_u\\) is the initial phase of the voltage and \\(\\varphi_i\\) is the initial phase of the electric current."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricPolarization qudt:latexDefinition "\\(P =\\frac{dp}{dV}\\), where \\(p\\) is electic charge density and \\(V\\) is volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ModulusOfElasticity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(E = \\frac{\\sigma}{\\varepsilon}\\), where \\(\\sigma\\) is the normal stress and \\(\\varepsilon\\) is the linear strain."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:PoissonRatio qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mu = \\frac{\\Delta \\delta}{\\Delta l}\\), where \\(\\Delta \\delta\\) is the lateral contraction and \\(\\Delta l\\) is the elongation."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:IsentropicExponent qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\varkappa = -\\frac{V}{p}\\left \\{  \\frac{\\partial p}{\\partial  V}\\right \\}_S\\), where \\(V\\) is volume, \\(p\\) is pressure, and \\(S\\) is entropy."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Emissivity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\varepsilon = \\frac{M}{M_b}\\), where \\(M\\) is the radiant exitance of a thermal radiator and \\(M_b\\) is the radiant exitance of a blackbody at the same temperature."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:StressOpticCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "When a ray of light passes through a photoelastic material, its electromagnetic wave components are resolved along the two principal stress directions and each component experiences a different refractive index due to the birefringence. The difference in the refractive indices leads to a relative phase retardation between the two components. Assuming a thin specimen made of isotropic materials, where two-dimensional photoelasticity is applicable, the magnitude of the relative retardation is given by the stress-optic law \\(\\Delta ={\\frac {2\\pi t}{\\lambda }}C(\\sigma _{1}-\\sigma _{2})\\), where \\(\\Delta\\) is the induced retardation, \\(C\\) is the stress-optic coefficient, \\(t\\) is the specimen thickness, \\(\\lambda\\) is the vacuum wavelength, and \\(\\sigma_1\\) and \\(\\sigma_2\\) are the first and second principal stresses, respectively."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Slowing-DownDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(q = -\\frac{dn}{dt}\\), where \\(n\\) is the number density and \\(dt\\) is the duration."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L0I0M1H0T-3D-1 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(U^-1 M T^-3\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime -3 .

qkdv:A0E0L3I0M1H0T-1D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^3 M T^-1\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime -1 .

qudtqk:HallCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "In an isotropic conductor, the relation between electric field strength, \\(E\\), and electric current density, \\(J\\) is \\(E = \\rho J + R_H(B X J)\\), where \\(\\rho\\) is resistivity, and \\(B\\) is magnetic flux density."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SoundIntensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(I = pv\\), where \\(p\\) is the sound pressure and \\(v\\) is sound particle velocity."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AverageEnergyLossPerElementaryChargeProduced qudt:latexDefinition "\\(W_i = \\frac{E_k}{N_i}\\), where \\(E_k\\) is the initial kinetic energy of an ionizing charged particle and \\(N_i\\) is the total ionization produced by that particle."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AtomicAttenuationCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mu_a = -\\frac{\\mu}{n}\\), where \\(\\mu\\) is the linear attenuation coefficient and \\(n\\) is the number density of the atoms in the substance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L0I0M0H0T2D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(T^2\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 2 .

qudtqk:KineticEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(T = \\frac{mv^2}{2}\\), where \\(m\\) is mass and \\(v\\) is speed."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:GroupSpeedOfSound qudt:latexDefinition "\\(c_g = \\frac{d\\omega}{dk}\\), where \\(\\omega\\) is the angular frequency and \\(k\\) is angular wavenumber."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:NuclearRadius qudt:latexDefinition "This quantity is not exactly defined. It is given approximately for nuclei in their ground state only by \\(R = r_0 A^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\), where \\(r_0 \\approx 1.2 x 10^{-15} m\\) and \\(A\\) is the nucleon number."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AbsoluteHumidity qudt:latexDefinition """\\(AH = \\frac{\\mathcal{M}_\\omega}{\\vee_{net}}\\),
where \\(\\mathcal{M}_\\omega\\) is the mass of water vapor per unit volume of total air and \\(\\vee_{net}\\) is water vapor mixture."""^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Kerma qudt:latexDefinition "For indirectly ionizing (uncharged) particles, \\(K= \\frac{dE_{tr}}{dm}\\), where \\(dE_{tr}\\) is the mean sum of the initial kinetic energies of all the charged ionizing particles liberated by uncharged ionizing particles in an element of matter, and \\(dm\\) is the mass of that element."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MolalityOfSolute qudt:latexDefinition "\\(b_B = \\frac{n_B}{m_a}\\), where \\(n_B\\) is the amount of substance and \\(m_A\\) is the mass."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:NuclearSpinQuantumNumber qudt:latexDefinition "\\(I^2 = \\hbar^2 I(I + 1)\\), where \\(\\hbar\\) is the Planck constant."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpinQuantumNumber qudt:latexDefinition "\\(s^2 = \\hbar^2 s(s + 1)\\), where \\(s\\) is the spin quantum number and \\(\\hbar\\) is the Planck constant."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:MOHM qudt:latexDefinition "\\(1\\:{mohm_{mks}} = 10^{3}\\:\\frac m {N.s}\\:(=\\:10^{3}\\:   \\frac s {kg}\\:in\\:base\\:m.k.s.\\:terms)\\)"^^qudt:LatexString,
    "\\(1\\:{mohm_{cgs}} = 1\\:\\frac {cm} {dyn.s}\\: (=\\:1\\:\\frac s g \\:in\\:base\\:c.g.s.\\:terms)\\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MeanMassRange qudt:latexDefinition "\\(R_\\rho = R\\rho\\), where \\(R\\) is the mean linear range and \\(\\rho\\) is the mass density of the sample."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ChemicalPotential qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mu_B = (\\frac{\\partial G}{\\partial n_B})_{T,p,n_i}\\), where \\(G\\) is Gibbs energy, and \\(n_B\\) is the amount of substance \\(B\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:NuclearQuadrupoleMoment qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Q = (\\frac{1}{e}) \\int (3z^2 - r^2)\\rho(x, y, z)dV\\), in the quantum state with the nuclear spin in the field direction \\((z)\\), where \\(\\rho(x, y, z)\\) is the nuclear electric charge density, \\(e\\) is the elementary charge, \\(r^2 = x^2 + y^2 + z^2\\), and \\(dV\\) is the volume element \\(dx\\) \\(dy\\) \\(dz\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L-1I0M0H-1T-2D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^-1 T^-2 Θ^-1\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime -2 .

qudtqk:RestEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "For a particle, \\(E_0 = m_0 c_0^2\\), where \\(m_0\\) is the rest mass of that particle, and \\(c_0\\) is the speed of light in vacuum."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E2L2I0M-1H0T2D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^2 M^-1 T^2 I^2\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 2;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 2 .

qkdv:A0E0L-2I0M-1H0T2D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^-2 M^-1 T^2\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 2 .

qudtqk:DiffusionCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(C_B \\left \\langle \\nu_B \\right \\rangle = -D grad C_B\\), where \\(C_B\\) the local molecular concentration of substance \\(B\\) in the mixture and \\(\\left \\langle \\nu_B \\right \\rangle\\) is the local average velocity of the molecules of \\(B\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MolarEntropy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(S_m = \\frac{S}{n}\\), where \\(S\\) is entropy and \\(n\\) is amount of substance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:PotentialEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(V = -\\int F \\cdot dr\\), where \\(F\\) is a conservative force and \\(R\\) is a position vector."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:HartreeEnergy qudt:latexDefinition "\\(E_H= \\frac{e^2}{4\\pi \\varepsilon_0 a_0 }\\), where \\(e\\) is the elementary charge, \\(\\varepsilon_0\\) is the electric constant, and \\(a_0\\) is the Bohr radius."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ElectricPolarizability qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\alpha_{i,j} = \\frac{\\partial p_i}{\\partial E_j}\\), where \\(p_i\\) is the cartesian component along the \\(i-axis\\) of the electric dipole moment induced by the applied electric field strength acting on the molecule, and \\(E_j\\) is the component along the \\(j-axis\\) of this electric field strength."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:CharacteristicAcousticImpedance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Z_c = pc\\), where \\(p\\) is the sound pressure and \\(c\\) is the phase speed of sound."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L0.5I0M0.5TE0TM-1D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^0.5 M^0.5 T^-1\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime -1 .

qudtqk:OsmoticPressure qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\varphi = -(M_A\\sum b_B)^{-1} \\ln a_A\\), where \\(M_A\\) is the molar mass of the solvent \\(A\\), \\(\\sum\\) denotes summation over all the solutes, \\(b_B\\) is the molality of solute \\(B\\), and \\(a_A\\) is the activity of solvent \\(A\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:EffectiveMass qudt:latexDefinition "\\(m^* = \\hbar^2k(\\frac{d\\varepsilon}{dk})\\), where \\(\\hbar\\) is the reduced Planck constant, \\(k\\) is the wavenumber, and \\(\\varepsilon\\) is the energy of the electron."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:FineStructureConstant qudt:latexDefinition "\\(a = \\frac{e^2}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0\\hbar c_0}\\), where \\(e\\) is the elementary charge, \\(\\varepsilon_0\\) is the electric constant, item \\(\\hbar\\) is the reduced Planck constant, and \\(c_0\\) is the speed of light in vacuum."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Dissipance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\delta = \\frac{P_d}{P_i}\\), where \\(P_d\\) is the dissipated sound power, and \\(P_i\\) is the incident sound power."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:ReducedPlanckConstant qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\hbar = \\frac{h}{2\\pi}\\), where \\(h\\) is the Planck constant."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:PlanckConstant qudt:latexDefinition "\\(E = h\\nu = \\frac{hc}{\\lambda}\\), where \\(E\\) is energy, \\(\\nu\\) is frequency, \\(\\lambda\\) is wavelength, and \\(c\\) is the speed of light."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MolecularConcentration qudt:latexDefinition "\\(C_B = \\frac{N_B}{V}\\), where \\(N_B\\) is the number of molecules of \\(B\\) and \\(V\\) is the volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MadelungConstant qudt:latexDefinition "For a uni-univalent ionic crystal of specified structure, the binding energy \\(V_b\\) per pair of ions is \\(V_b = \\alpha\\frac{e^2}{4\\pi \\varepsilon_0 a}\\), where \\(e\\) is the elementary charge, \\(\\varepsilon_0\\) is the electric constant, and \\(a\\) is the lattice constant which should be specified."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E-1L1I0M0H0T0D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L I^-1\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent -1;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 0 .

constant:NuclearMagneton qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\mu_N = \\frac{e\\hbar}{2m_p}\\), where \\(e\\) is the elementary charge, \\(\\hbar\\) is the Planck constant, and \\(m_p\\) is the rest mass of proton."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:BohrRadius qudt:latexDefinition "\\(a_0 = \\frac{4\\pi \\varepsilon_0 \\hbar^2}{m_ee^2}\\), where \\(\\varepsilon_0\\) is the electric constant, \\(\\hbar\\) is the reduced Planck constant, \\(m_e\\)  is the rest mass of electron, and \\(e\\) is the elementary charge."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:OrbitalAngularMomentumQuantumNumber qudt:latexDefinition "\\(l^2 = \\hbar^2 l(l + 1), l = 0, 1, ..., n - 1\\), where \\(l_i\\) refers to a specific particle \\(i\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:RelativeMassExcess qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Delta_r = \\frac{\\Delta}{m_u}\\), where \\(\\Delta\\) is the mass excess and \\(m_u\\) is the unified atomic mass constant."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AreicHeatFlowRate qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\varphi = \\frac{\\Phi}{A}\\), where \\(\\Phi\\) is heat flow rate and \\(A\\) is area."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpecificOpticalRotatoryPower qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\alpha_m = \\alpha \\frac{A}{m}\\), where \\(\\alpha\\) is the angle of optical rotation, and \\(m\\) is the mass of the optically active component in the path of a linearly polarized light beam of cross sectional area \\(A\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L0I0M1H0T2D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(M T^2\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 2 .

qudtqk:ParticleFluenceRate qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\theta = \\frac{d\\Phi}{dt}\\), where \\(d\\Phi\\) is the increment of the particle fluence during an infinitesimal time interval with duration \\(dt\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LondonPenetrationDepth qudt:latexDefinition "If an applied magnetic field is parallel to the plane surface of a semi-infinite superconductor, the field penetrates the superconductor according to the expression \\(B(x) = B(0) \\exp{(\\frac{-x}{\\lambda_L})}\\), where \\(B\\) is magnetic flux density and \\(x\\) is the distance from the surface."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Wavenumber qudt:latexDefinition """\\(\\sigma = \\frac{\\nu}{c}\\), where \\(\\sigma\\) is the wave number, \\(\\nu\\) is the frequency, and \\(c\\) is the speed of light in the medium.

Or:

\\(k = \\frac{2\\pi}{\\lambda}= \\frac{2\\pi\\upsilon}{\\upsilon_p}=\\frac{\\omega}{\\upsilon_p}\\), where \\(\\upsilon\\) is the frequency of the wave, \\(\\lambda\\) is the wavelength, \\(\\omega = 2\\pi \\upsilon\\) is the angular frequency of the wave, and \\(\\upsilon_p\\) is the phase velocity of the wave."""^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MacroscopicCrossSection qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\sum = n_1\\sigma_1 + \\cdots + n_j\\sigma_j +\\), where \\(n_j\\) is the number density and \\(\\sigma_j\\) the cross-section for entities of type \\(j\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpecificEnergyImparted qudt:latexDefinition "For ionizing radiation, \\(z = \\frac{\\varepsilon}{m}\\), where \\(\\varepsilon\\) is the energy imparted to irradiated matter and \\(m\\) is the mass of that matter."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:RydbergConstant qudt:latexDefinition "\\(R_\\infty = \\frac{e^2}{8\\pi \\varepsilon_0 a_0 h c_0 }\\), where \\(e\\) is the elementary charge, \\(\\varepsilon_0\\) is the electric constant, \\(a_0\\) is the Bohr radius, \\(h\\) is the Planck constant, and \\(c_0\\) is the speed of light in vacuum."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SurfaceCoefficientOfHeatTransfer qudt:latexDefinition "\\(q = h (T_s - T_r)\\), where \\(T_s\\) is areic heat flow rate is the thermodynamic temperature of the surface, and is a reference thermodynamic temperature characteristic of the adjacent surroundings."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassFraction qudt:latexDefinition "\\(w_B = \\frac{m_B}{m}\\), where \\(m_B\\) is the mass of substance \\(B\\) and \\(m\\) is the total."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L-1.5I0M0.5TE0TM-1D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^-1.5 M^0.5 T^-1\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime -1 .

qudtqk:OsmoticCoefficient qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\varphi = -(M_A\\sum b_B)^{-1} \\ln a_A\\), where \\(M_A\\) is the molar mass of the solvent \\(A\\), \\(\\sum\\) denotes summation over all the solutes, \\(b_B\\) is the molality of solute \\(B\\), and \\(a_A\\) is the activity of solvent \\(A\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:BraggAngle qudt:latexDefinition "\\(2d\\sin{\\vartheta} = n\\lambda \\)"^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LinearDensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\rho_l = \\frac{dm}{dl}\\), where \\(m\\) is mass and \\(l\\) is length."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MigrationLength qudt:latexDefinition "\\(M = \\sqrt{M^2}\\), where \\(M^2\\) is the migration area."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:GruneisenParameter qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\gamma = \\frac{\\alpha_V}{x_T c_V\\rho}\\), where \\(\\alpha_V\\) is the cubic expansion coefficient, \\(x_T\\) is isothermal compressibility, \\(c_V\\) is specific heat capacity at constant volume, and \\(\\rho\\) is mass density."^^qudt:LatexString .

unit:ST qudt:latexDefinition "\\((cm^2/s\\))"^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L-0.5I0M0.5TE0TM-2D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^-0.5 M^0.5 T^-2\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime -2 .

qkdv:A0E4L-5I0M-3H0T10D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^-5 M^-3 T^10 I^4\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 4;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 10 .

qkdv:A0E0L4I0M1H0T-3D-1 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(U^-1 L^4 M T^-3\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime -3 .

qkdv:A0E0L2I0M1H0T-3D-1 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(U^-1 L^2 M T^-3\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime -3 .

qudtqk:LinkedFlux qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Psi_m = \\int_C A \\cdot dr\\), where \\(A\\) is magnetic vector potential and \\(dr\\) is the vector element of the curve \\(C\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MachNumber qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Ma = \\frac{v_o}{c_o}\\), where \\(v_0\\) is speed, and \\(c_o\\) is speed of sound."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AmountOfSubstanceConcentrationOfB qudt:latexDefinition "\\(C_B = \\frac{n_B}{V}\\), where \\(n_B\\) is the amount of substance \\(B\\) and \\(V\\) is the volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E1L-2I0M-1H0T3D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^-2 M^-1 T^3 I\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 1;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 3 .

qudtqk:Debye-WallerFactor qudt:latexDefinition "\\(u = R - R_0\\), where \\(R\\) is the particle position vector and \\(R_0\\) is the equilibrium position vector of a particle."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Reactivity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\rho = \\frac{k_{eff} - 1}{k_{eff}}\\), where \\(k_{eff}\\) is the effective multiplication factor."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:GFactorOfNucleus qudt:latexDefinition "\\(g = \\frac{\\mu}{I\\mu_B}\\), where \\(\\mu\\) is the magnitude of magnetic dipole moment, \\(I\\) is the nuclear angular momentum quantum number, and \\(\\mu_B\\) is the Bohr magneton."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:PackingFraction qudt:latexDefinition "\\(f = \\frac{\\Delta_r}{A}\\), where \\(\\Delta_r\\) is the relative mass excess and \\(A\\) is the nucleon number."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:BindingFraction qudt:latexDefinition "\\(b = \\frac{B_r}{A}\\), where \\(B_r\\) is the relative mass defect and \\(A\\) is the nucleon number."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:StandardAbsoluteActivity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\lambda_B^\\Theta = \\lambda_B^*(p^\\Theta)\\), where \\(\\lambda_B^\\Theta\\) the absolute activity of the pure substance \\(B\\) at the same temperature and pressure, and \\(p^\\Theta\\) is standard pressure."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Irradiance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(E = \\frac{d\\Phi}{dA}\\), where \\(d\\Phi\\) is the radiant flux incident on an element of the surface with area \\(dA\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:TimeAveragedSoundIntensity qudt:latexDefinition "\\(I = \\frac{1}{t2 - t1} \\int_{t1}^{t2}i(t)dt\\), where \\(t1\\) and \\(t2\\) are the starting and ending times for the integral and \\(i\\) is sound intensity."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L0.5I0M0.5TE0TM0D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^0.5 M^0.5\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 0 .

qkdv:A0E0L-2I0M0H0T2D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^{-2} T^2\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 2 .

qudtqk:MicroCanonicalPartitionFunction qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Omega = \\sum_r 1\\), where the sum is over all quantum states consistent with given energy. volume, external fields, and content."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:ReynoldsNumber qudt:latexDefinition "\\(Re = \\frac{\\rho uL}{\\mu} = \\frac{uL}{\\nu}\\), where \\(\\rho\\) is mass density, \\(u\\) is speed, \\(L\\) is length,  \\(\\mu\\) is dynamic viscosity, and \\(\\nu\\) is kinematic viscosity."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:Landau-GinzburgNumber qudt:latexDefinition "At zero thermodynamic temperature \\(\\kappa = \\frac{\\lambda_L}{(\\varepsilon\\sqrt{2})}\\), where \\(\\lambda_L\\) is London penetration depth and \\(\\varepsilon\\) is coherence length."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:MassNumber qudt:latexDefinition "\\(A = Z + N\\), where \\(Z\\) is the atomic number and \\(N\\) is the neutron number."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:MagneticFluxQuantum qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Phi_0 = \\frac{h}{2e}\\), where \\(h\\) is the Planck constant and \\(e\\) is the elementary charge."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L-1.5I0M0.5TE0TM0D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^-1.5 M^0.5\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 0 .

constant:AvogadroConstant qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L = \\frac{N}{n}\\), where \\(N\\) is the number of particles and \\(n\\) is amount of substance."^^qudt:LatexString .

constant:Pi qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\pi = \\frac{C}{d}\\), where \\(C\\) is the circumference of a circle and \\(d\\) is the diameter of a circle."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L0I0M0H0T-1D1 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(U T^-1\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime -1 .

qkdv:A0E0L-2I1M-1H0T3D1 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(U L^-2 M^-1 T^3 J\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 1;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime 3 .

qudtqk:RadiantEmmitance qudt:latexDefinition "\\(M = \\frac{d\\Phi}{dA}\\), where \\(d\\Phi\\) is the radiant flux leaving the element of the surface area \\(dA\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:EnergyFluenceRate qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\Psi = \\frac{d\\Psi}{dt}\\), where \\(d\\Psi\\) is the increment of the energy fluence during an infinitesimal time interval with duration \\(dt\\)."^^qudt:LatexString .

qkdv:A0E0L-0.5I0M0.5TE0TM-1D0 qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L^-0.5 M^0.5 T^-1\\)"^^qudt:LatexString;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForLuminousIntensity 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForElectricCurrent 0;
  qudt:dimensionExponentForTime -1 .

qudtqk:PartialPressure qudt:latexDefinition "\\(p_B = x_B \\cdot p\\), where \\(x_B\\) is the amount-of-substance fraction of substance \\(B\\) and \\(p\\) is the total pressure."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:EnergyImparted qudt:latexDefinition "For ionizing radiation in the matter in a given 3D domain, \\(\\varepsilon = \\sum_i \\varepsilon_i\\), where the energy deposit, \\(\\varepsilon_i\\) is the energy deposited in a single interaction \\(i\\), and is given by \\(\\varepsilon_i = \\varepsilon_{in} - \\varepsilon_{out} + Q\\), where \\(\\varepsilon_{in}\\) is the energy of the incident ionizing particle, excluding rest energy, \\(\\varepsilon_{out}\\) is the sum of the energies of all ionizing particles leaving the interaction, excluding rest energy, and \\(Q\\) is the change in the rest energies of the nucleus and of all particles involved in the interaction."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SolidStateDiffusionLength qudt:latexDefinition "\\(L = \\sqrt{D\\tau}\\), where \\(D\\) is the diffusion coefficient and \\(\\tau\\) is lifetime."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:CyclotronAngularFrequency qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\omega_c = \\frac{\\left | q \\right |}{m}B\\), where \\(q\\) is the electric charge, \\(m\\) is its mass, and \\(B\\) is the magnetic flux density."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:LossAngle qudt:latexDefinition "\\(\\delta = \\arctan d\\), where \\(d\\) is loss factor."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AmountOfSubstanceConcentration qudt:latexDefinition "\\(C_B = \\frac{n_B}{V}\\), where \\(n_B\\) is the amount of substance \\(B\\) and \\(V\\) is the volume."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:AmountOfSubstanceFraction qudt:latexDefinition "\\(x_B = \\frac{n_B}{n}\\), where \\(n_B\\) is the amount of substance \\(B\\) and \\(n\\) is the total amount of substance."^^qudt:LatexString .

qudtqk:SpecificSurfaceArea qudt:latexDefinition "\\(SSA = \\frac{SA}{\\m}\\), where \\(SA\\) is the surface area of an object and \\(\\m\\) is the mass density of the object."^^qudt:LatexString .

